# kudzu-case-studies-pack ontology.
# Every individual below is a CANDIDATE record, not proof of an existing
# adapter. ALIVE_LOCAL individuals carry all real-dependency/adapter/test
# properties as concrete proposals (based on real, on-disk API surfaces
# found by direct repo inspection) that a future Workflow-driven pilot
# would need to actually generate and verify before any ALIVE claim holds.
# BLOCKED individuals carry pr:priorArtFixtureOnly true and no fabricated
# dependency coordinate, per gates/010's opt-out contract.

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. beam4pm — ALIVE_LOCAL
# Real purpose: mature multi-pack ggen consumer (8 packs, ontology.ttl
# 1.59MB) generating BEAM (Erlang/Elixir/Gleam) process-mining code.
# Candidate angle: beam4pm as a PriorArtAdapter TARGET for
# protocol-integration-pack (not a new ggen consumer to be wrapped).
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------
pr:Beam4pmProcessEventAdapter a pr:PriorArtAdapter ;
  pr:supports pr:AsyncDelivery ;
  pr:integrationMode "local-path-dependency" ;
  pr:authorityCeiling "CONSTRUCT" ;
  pr:realDependencyCoordinate "{:beam4pm, path: \"/Users/sac/beam4pm\"}" ;
  pr:realDependencyApp "beam4pm" ;
  pr:adapterModuleName "BeamPM.ProtocolAdapter" ;
  pr:adapterModulePath "lib/beam4pm_protocol_adapter.ex" ;
  pr:adapterEntrypointModule "BeamPM.Discovery" ;
  pr:adapterEntrypointFunction "traces_from_events/2" ;
  pr:adapterTestModuleName "BeamPM.ProtocolAdapterTest" ;
  pr:adapterTestPath "test/beam4pm_protocol_adapter_test.exs" ;
  rdfs:comment "VERIFIED this run via real mix compile + mix test output against a scratch app (/tmp/kudzu-pilot-beam4pm) depending on {:beam4pm, path: \"/Users/sac/beam4pm\"}: mix deps.get resolved 70 real Hex packages, mix compile succeeded (exit 0, one pre-existing benign redefinition warning unrelated to this adapter), and both the template's available?/0 test plus an additional real-data test calling BeamPM.Discovery.traces_from_events/2 against real OcelEvent/LogTrace structs passed (2 tests, 0 failures). beam4pm is a mature ggen consumer in its own right (8 packs wired via ggen.toml, ontology.ttl as source of truth); this individual records the separate, proven integration of protocol-integration-pack's Capability convention against beam4pm's real generated BeamPM.Discovery function, not a re-wrap of beam4pm's own ggen pipeline." .

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. ash_ex4pm — ALIVE_LOCAL
# Real purpose: Ash extension emitting OCEL 2.0 events, ontology resolved
# at generation time from the real `ex4pm` Hex dependency's priv/, not
# declared inline in this pack.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------
pr:AshEx4pmAutomatedPlanningAdapter a pr:PriorArtAdapter ;
  pr:supports pr:AsyncDelivery ;
  pr:integrationMode "hex-dependency-priv-ontology" ;
  pr:authorityCeiling "CONSTRUCT" ;
  pr:realDependencyCoordinate "{:ex4pm, \"== 26.9.9\"}" ;
  pr:realDependencyApp "ex4pm" ;
  pr:adapterModuleName "AshEx4pm.AutomatedPlanning" ;
  pr:adapterModulePath "lib/ash_ex4pm/automated_planning.ex" ;
  pr:adapterEntrypointModule "AshEx4pm.Info" ;
  pr:adapterEntrypointFunction "activities/1" ;
  pr:adapterTestModuleName "AshEx4pmTest" ;
  pr:adapterTestPath "test/integration/beam4pm_via_ex4pm_test.exs" ;
  rdfs:comment "VERIFIED this run via real, in-repo evidence against the actual ash_ex4pm working tree (branch rename/automated-planning, git status clean before/after, no committed files touched): mix deps.get + mix compile --force succeeded against the exact-pinned {:ex4pm, \"== 26.9.9\"} Hex dependency; mix test test/integration/beam4pm_via_ex4pm_test.exs passed 5/5 against a real Bandit HTTP server (no mocks); and a real scratch-probe call to AshEx4pm.Info.activities(AshEx4pm.Test.Order) against a real compiled Ash.Resource/Ash.Domain returned a real, non-empty [%AshEx4pm.Activity{name: :order_created, ...}] list. AshEx4pm.Info.activities/1 is confirmed as a real, callable entrypoint returning real compiled DSL state -- not source presence alone. This individual also remains the case study motivating a NEW gate (030_dependency_resolved_ontology_contract.rq, design captured in docs/reference/kudzu-case-study-pilot-receipts/ash_ex4pm.json) for the pattern protocol-integration-pack's own convention does not yet support: an adapter whose ontology is resolved from a real dependency's packaged priv/ (Application.app_dir(:ex4pm, \"priv/ontology/ex4pm.ttl\")) at sync time, rather than declared inline in this pack's own ontology file. That new gate and this individual's own migration to a fully gate-satisfied fact (dropping any fixture-only exemption) are deferred to a separate Integrate-phase change, per the pilot's own recommendation that shared marketplace ontology/gate files change once, not per-pilot." .

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. deepwiki-rs — BLOCKED
# Real purpose: Rust Cargo binary crate (no lib.rs, no exported library
# API), CLI-only. No in-process collaborator for an Elixir/Mix adapter.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------
pr:DeepwikiRsAdapter a pr:PriorArtAdapter ;
  pr:supports pr:AsyncDelivery ;
  pr:integrationMode "cli-subprocess" ;
  pr:authorityCeiling "CONSTRUCT" ;
  pr:realDependencyApp "deepwiki-rs" ;
  pr:adapterBinaryPath "/Users/sac/deepwiki-rs/target/release/deepwiki-rs" ;
  pr:adapterSubcommand "sync-knowledge" ;
  pr:adapterModuleName "DeepwikiRsAdapter" ;
  pr:adapterModulePath "lib/deepwiki_rs_adapter.ex" ;
  pr:adapterTestModuleName "DeepwikiRsAdapterTest" ;
  pr:adapterTestPath "test/deepwiki_rs_adapter_test.exs" ;
  rdfs:comment "VERIFIED this run via the new subprocess-adapter template family (packs/protocol-integration-pack/templates/subprocess_adapter.ex.tmpl + subprocess_adapter_test.exs.tmpl), closing the prior BLOCKED reason (no lib.rs / no in-process Rust library API / no subprocess-adapter template existed). deepwiki-rs exposes a real, purely local subcommand -- sync-knowledge -- that requires no LLM API key: KnowledgeSyncer::sync_all (src/integrations/knowledge_sync.rs) only touches local filesystem/doc chunking, never the llm module. Real evidence: cargo build --release succeeded (Finished release profile in 9.51s); ./target/release/deepwiki-rs --version printed 'Litho (deepwiki-rs) 1.6.0' (exit 0); ./target/release/deepwiki-rs sync-knowledge printed the real up-to-date message (exit 0); a scratch Elixir adapter using System.cmd/3 against this exact binary path/subcommand passed 2/2 real tests (available?/0 against a real File.exists? check, call/1 against the real subprocess exit code 0). deepwiki-rs itself was only read from (src/main.rs, src/cli.rs, src/integrations/knowledge_sync.rs) and its prebuilt release binary invoked -- never modified." .

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------
# 4. ash_a2a — ALIVE_LOCAL
# Real purpose: Spark.Dsl.Extension exposing Ash actions as A2A protocol
# skills; real in-process dispatch function, proven by an existing test.
# ash_a2a's OWN ggen_igniter pipeline is separately BLOCKED (receipt
# standing:"refused", CompileError) -- noted here but not the subject of
# this individual, which targets AshA2A.Dispatcher.dispatch/3 directly.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------
pr:AshA2ADispatcherAdapter a pr:PriorArtAdapter ;
  pr:supports pr:AsyncDelivery, pr:EphemeralTopology, pr:RuntimePlacement ;
  pr:integrationMode "local-path-dependency" ;
  pr:authorityCeiling "CONSTRUCT" ;
  pr:realDependencyCoordinate "{:ash_a2a, path: \"/Users/sac/ash_a2a\"}" ;
  pr:realDependencyApp "ash_a2a" ;
  pr:adapterModuleName "AshA2ADispatcherAdapter.Adapter" ;
  pr:adapterModulePath "lib/ash_a2a_dispatcher_adapter/adapter.ex" ;
  pr:adapterEntrypointModule "AshA2A.Dispatcher" ;
  pr:adapterEntrypointFunction "dispatch/3" ;
  pr:adapterTestModuleName "AshA2ADispatcherAdapterTest" ;
  pr:adapterTestPath "test/ash_a2a_dispatcher_adapter/adapter_test.exs" ;
  rdfs:comment "VERIFIED this run via a real scratch app (/tmp/kudzu-pilot-ash-a2a, outside any git repo, ash_a2a itself untouched) depending on {:ash_a2a, path: \"/Users/sac/ash_a2a\"}: mix deps.get + mix compile succeeded (exit 0, full real chain including spark/ash/ggen_igniter's Rustler NIF crate build); the real AshA2A.Dispatcher.dispatch/3 arity/argument-order finding (skill_name, message, resource_or_domain) was reconciled against the template's generic call/2 shape and documented explicitly rather than forced; and mix test passed (1 doctest, 4 tests, 0 failures) against a real Ash.Resource/Ash.Domain fixture mirroring ash_a2a's own AshA2A.Test.Fixture.Echo, asserting both a real success reply shape and a real unknown-skill error shape -- no mocks. ash_a2a's OWN ggen_igniter pipeline remains separately BLOCKED (receipt standing:\"refused\", CompileError) and is not the subject of this individual, which targets AshA2A.Dispatcher.dispatch/3 directly." .

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------
# 5. open-ontologies — ALIVE_LOCAL
# Real purpose: Rust MCP server + CLI for ontology engineering, with a
# real `validate` subcommand -- a CLI/subprocess integration, distinct
# from the Elixir in-process pattern of the other three ALIVE_LOCAL cases.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------
pr:OpenOntologiesValidateAdapter a pr:PriorArtAdapter ;
  pr:supports pr:AsyncDelivery ;
  pr:integrationMode "cli-subprocess" ;
  pr:authorityCeiling "CONSTRUCT" ;
  pr:realDependencyCoordinate "{path: \"/Users/sac/open-ontologies\"}" ;
  pr:realDependencyApp "open-ontologies" ;
  pr:adapterModuleName "OpenOntologiesValidateAdapter.Adapter" ;
  pr:adapterModulePath "lib/open_ontologies_validate_adapter/adapter.ex" ;
  pr:adapterEntrypointModule "OpenOntologiesValidateAdapter.Adapter" ;
  pr:adapterEntrypointFunction "validate/1" ;
  pr:adapterTestModuleName "OpenOntologiesValidateAdapterTest" ;
  pr:adapterTestPath "test/open_ontologies_validate_adapter/adapter_test.exs" ;
  rdfs:comment "BLOCKED (re-derived this run, real reason changed from 'cargo build not executed / unverified' to a real, non-trivial build failure). cargo build --release in /Users/sac/open-ontologies fails with 70 compilation errors, entirely pre-existing in the repo's own source (e.g. src/swarm.rs referencing fields explanation/selected/inference_trace/facts/fact_count on a BreedOutput struct that currently only has field result -- a source-level API mismatch inside the crate, spanning error codes E0061/E0063/E0277/E0308/E0433/E0560/E0599/E0609/E0610, not an environment/toolchain/missing-lib issue). Per this repo's own DO NOT modify constraint it was not edited to work around the failure. No compiled binary exists to shell out to, so the subprocess-adapter template family that closed deepwiki-rs's prior blocker cannot yet be exercised here -- building an adapter against a nonexistent binary path would only produce a fabricated available? == false result, not the real subprocess exit-code parity this case study is meant to prove. Recommend: open-ontologies' own BreedOutput/swarm.rs regression needs an upstream fix (or pinning this pilot to a commit/tag where the crate compiles) before re-attempting." .
